usergroup_release: posixc must release usergroup.library at program exit
==========================================================================

posixc opens usergroup.library on the first getpw*() / getgr*() call and
keeps it until its own base is finally closed. usergroup holds a reference
on that same per-task posixc base (`rellib posixc`), so the final close never
came: every program that looked up a user left its posixc and usergroup
bases open, and a later program in the same process could be handed the
stale posixc base.

Native test (registered in the posixc test build)
-------------------------------------------------

    usergroup_release          runs usergroup_release_child three times with
    usergroup_release_child    RunCommand(), in its own process, and compares
                               the open counts of usergroup.library and
                               posixc.library before and after.

Both programs must be in the same directory. The parent does not use posixc
itself and opens usergroup.library first, so that the child never performs
the library's first load (a separate case, see the genmodule option
norootrellibs). Expected output:

    USERGROUP RELEASE PASS: runs=3 child_rc=0 usergroup N->N posixc M->M

Before the fix both counts grow. They grow by one per invocation rather than
per child run: the three runs start from the same point in the same process,
so the second and third are handed the base the first one left behind, which
is the defect itself. The counts are system-wide:
another program opening or closing posixc.library while the test runs can
disturb them, so run it on an otherwise idle system.

Host test
---------

    usergroup_release_host.sh <AROS source tree> [compiler [compiler-arg...]]

Compiles posixc's __optionallibs.c and stdc's __exitfunc.c unchanged on the
host, against the stand-in headers in usergroup_release_host/, and checks:

    release  the release runs from the program's exit list, after exit
             handlers registered earlier (which may still read a struct passwd)
    nostdc   without the program's C library base nothing is queued and
             usergroup stays open until __optionallibs_close, as before
    nomem    if the exit-list node cannot be allocated, the open is undone and
             usergroup is reported unavailable
    noopen   if usergroup.library cannot be opened, nothing is queued

The compiler is given as the command followed by its own arguments, one word
per argument; it defaults to cc, and CC in the environment is not used. The
source tree and the compiler may be in directories whose names contain spaces.

It passes with -Wall -Wextra -Werror, and under the sanitizers:

    usergroup_release_host.sh <AROS source tree> \
        cc -fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all
